This folder contains the CMake modules and scripts of the Geneva build: the
shared functionality of the build (CommonGenevaBuild.cmake and the modules it
includes), the helpers of the test suite (the Check*.cmake drivers, the
registration of tests that start MPI jobs with GenevaMpiTest.cmake and its
runner GenevaRunMpiTest.sh, the size labels, the best-of-N runs), and the
templates of what an installation carries. Each file says at its top what it
is for.

What an installation carries from here:

- FindGeneva.cmake, generated from FindGeneva.cmake.in when Geneva is built:
  the only module installed into the installation's CMakeModules/ directory,
  the MODULE-mode fallback for finding an installed Geneva;
- the config package (GenevaConfig.cmake, generated from GenevaConfig.cmake.in,
  with its version file), which carries its own helpers next to it:
  GenevaIndividualModule.cmake, GenevaConfigMaterialization.cmake and
  GenevaRunQuiet.cmake (the install rule is in the top-level CMakeLists.txt).

Everything else builds and checks the collection itself; a project outside the
tree uses find_package(Geneva) instead.


See the files for licensing information.
